# "Enters tapped unless it's your turn" only ever sets tapped (CR 614.1d): it cannot untap a permanent that an instruction puts
# onto the battlefield tapped. Raph & Mikey attack on Bot1's own turn and put the first creature card revealed, Horned
# Loch-Whale, onto the battlefield tapped and attacking; it is Bot1's turn, so the Whale's own clause does nothing, and the
# Whale stays tapped. (The turn-1 scenario, cast untapped, is the control for the clause itself.)

[Bot1 Deck]
Mountain
Mox Ruby
Mox Emerald
Black Lotus
Sol Ring
Raph & Mikey, Troublemakers
Forest
Horned Loch-Whale
Forest
Forest

[Bot2 Deck]
Forest x14

[Actions]
